{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nThe evening air in The Hague is crisp, and I am already on the coach for Breda. I write to tell you of a curiosity I saw there: a tomb monument ascribed to Michelangelo. It is a striking piece, showing a count and his wife in white alabaster lying upon a black slab. Above them, four standing figures—Julius Caesar, Hannibal, and Regulus among them—support a second slab at the corners. It is a composition of great dignity, the dead held aloft by the weight of historical virtue. One cannot help but reflect on how the particular lives of these individuals are preserved within the universal structure of the state and history. The alabaster seems to glow against the dark stone, a quiet testament to the permanence of ethical life. I hope the boys are well and that your health holds steady. The journey continues, and I shall write again from the next post.\n\nYours ever,\nG.W.F. Hegel"}}],"created":1795080236,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":206,"prompt_tokens":943,"total_tokens":1149,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-NyQYWxtCtjZZ3V63teaHyUFwGZSdRdkX","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":943,"prompt_ms":935.721,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.9922810180275716,"prompt_per_second":1007.779028150485,"predicted_n":206,"predicted_ms":4957.674,"predicted_per_token_ms":24.183775609756097,"predicted_per_second":41.35003632751972}}